Subject: [PATCH] feat(M3.75): Policy-as-Code + Audit Events + Middleware +
 Explain rules_fired
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Phase 0 — Policy-as-Code foundation:
- Add PolicyConfig dataclass with 6 toggles (env-overridable)
- Add PolicyViolation exception for uniform error handling
- Add policy_guard() central gate for upload/export/explain validation
- Add ensure_audit_events_table() and policy_log_event() for audit trail
- Add audit_events table to core/db.py schema (idempotent)

Phase 1 — Policy middleware + exception handler:
- Add PolicyMiddleware (sets request_id, current_user, enforces auth
  on /snapshot/a/, /simulator/a/, /explain/a/, /history, /api/analyses/)
- Add uniform PolicyViolation exception handler (HTML for pages, JSON for /api/*)
- Add audit logging for login success/failure, register, upload, export, download

Phase 2 — Determinism + Explainability enforcement:
- Upload gate: policy_guard validates NaN fields, persistent ownership
- Trend compute failures audited (non-fatal, does not block upload)
- Export gate: audit export_record_failed events
- Explain engine returns rules_fired list (backward-compatible)
- New GET /api/analyses/{analysis_id}/explain endpoint with auth+ownership+rules_fired
- Fix pre-existing detect_rules import bug in app.py

